/*
  English texts of RoomEQ.

  Key = the Italian text written in the code (development language), with the
  values written as format specifiers: %@ (text), %lld / %llu / %u (whole
  numbers). The English text must keep the same specifiers, in the same order
  (or numbered: %1$@, %2$@…). Numbers arrive already formatted (decimal
  separator of the user's region); units (dB, Hz, kHz, ms) are not translated.
  Quotes: «» in Italian, “” in English.

  Checked at every build by tools/check-localizations.swift (missing keys,
  mismatched specifiers). Italian needs no translation, the key is the
  text: Resources/it.lproj/Localizable.strings is intentionally empty and
  only stops the lookup from falling back to this table.
*/

